                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Black Clover: Quartet Knights is a third person, team based action game built around four player roles: fighters, ranged attackers, supporters, and healers. Its original story follows a younger Yami and a new threat to the Clover Kingdom, giving fans a fresh anime style side story.\r\n\r\nThe cast is faithful to the series, and the different character roles give combat a team strategy angle. The magic abilities are easy to pick up, and the original story and familiar Japanese voices may be a draw for fans. \r\n\r\nThe campaign is short and super easy, and the fights can become repetitive. Some players I read say they found the game generic and unevenly balanced (which I get because there are some characters that feel way more OP compared to others). \r\n\r\nThe game was designed with online 4v4 battles in mind, so its lasting appeal depends on finding other players. The bad part is that the online community is very quiet (and pretty much not around, unless you search forums and ask around), the AI matches become more important for those who want to play online or have that online experience. \r\n\r\nA passable anime tie in with a fun premise, but limited depth and longevity. It’s easiest to recommend to Black Clover fans who can get it at a steep discount and mainly want the story and character roster. If you’re looking for a deep action game or a dependable online community, it’s a harder sell.",
